    "source": "taxguru-advance-tax-2025",
    "legacy_section": "207-211 (advance tax), 234B, 234C (interest)",
    "note": "Advance tax is due when tax payable after TDS is at least the threshold. Cumulative % of that tax is due by each date; deferment interest per month runs on the shortfall for the stated months, except that paying the safe-harbour % by the first two dates avoids it. Paying less than the year-end % attracts interest from 1 April of the assessment year until paid. The shortfall is rounded down to the rounding unit before interest (Rule 119A practice; an assumption under the 2025 Act). Tax on capital gains or dividends arising after an instalment date may be paid in the remaining instalments without deferment interest (not modelled)."
  },
